    {
      "id": "25325a3989dab64a",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Alexander Millington-Cotes is concerned for welfare of the 82-year-old, who hasn’t been seen in public for two years&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The stepson of Sir Ranulph Fiennes has launched a crowdfunder to pay for “specialist legal advice” in an attempt to locate the explorer, who hasn’t been seen in public for more than two years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Alexander Millington-Cotes, 31, has set a target of £55,000 for the fundraiser, to enable him to instruct lawyers to “locate and safeguard” Fiennes.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/26/ranulph-fiennes-explorer-stepson-launches-crowdfunder\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
